        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Fix Kimi rate limit ordering",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes Kimi's quota lane ordering so the short rate-limit window is shown before the weekly quota.\n\n- Maps Kimi rate limit usage to the primary lane and weekly quota to the secondary lane.\n- Updates Kimi labels to `Rate Limit` / `Weekly`.\n- Removes Kimi from the menu-bar resolver special case that preferred the secondary lane.\n- Treats malformed or non-positive Kimi rate-limit payloads as unavailable so weekly-only accounts still fall back to the weekly metric.\n- Adds regression coverage for menu-card ordering, parser conversion, weekly-only fallback, malformed rate limits, animation, and highest-usage selection.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nCurrent `main` had Kimi modeled backwards: weekly quota was stored as `primary`, rate limit was stored as `secondary`, and the automatic menu-bar metric special-cased Kimi to prefer the secondary lane. That made Kimi display weekly usage before the more constrained rate-limit window.\n\n## Relation To #1762\n\n#1762 includes the same invariant conceptually as part of broader Kimi Code work, but it remains open and explicitly held for additional gates. This PR is the narrow current-main fix for #1912 so the user-visible quota ordering can land independently.\n\nFixes #1912.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter KimiUsageSnapshotConversionTests`\n- `swift test --filter KimiUsageResponseParsingTests`\n- `make check`\n- Earlier full-suite validation before the final malformed-rate-limit hardening: `make test`",
